WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.040
[theme song playing]

00:47.280 --> 00:49.000
[Polly] Welcome to the opening

00:49.080 --> 00:54.760
of the Grace Shelby Institute
for the non-insured children of the poor.

00:55.480 --> 00:57.160
I would very much like you to join me

00:57.920 --> 01:02.760
in thanking the man that made the founding
of this establishment actually possible.

01:03.400 --> 01:05.200
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:06.160 --> 01:07.680
Mr. Thomas Shelby.

01:08.160 --> 01:09.680
[crowd applauding]

01:12.560 --> 01:14.160
[Arthur] Speech!

01:14.240 --> 01:16.280
Come on, speech!

01:23.960 --> 01:24.960
[baby crying]

01:25.200 --> 01:28.040
Say it, Tom. Say it to 'em!

01:29.480 --> 01:30.880
[John] Lay the foundation!

01:32.520 --> 01:33.520
[indistinct chatter]

01:38.320 --> 01:41.200
Um, I didn't come here today
to make a speech, but I will say this.

01:41.560 --> 01:43.720
These children are now safe.

01:44.200 --> 01:46.880
In our care, they will be safe.

01:47.480 --> 01:50.920
Because we are from the same cold streets
as they are.

01:51.160 --> 01:53.040
And in our care,

01:53.120 --> 01:56.000
they won't be shipped away
to the colonies.

01:56.760 --> 01:58.600
Or separated from kin.

01:59.080 --> 02:02.760
Or made to work for men
in their various ways.

02:03.600 --> 02:06.440
They will grow up here. At home.

02:07.360 --> 02:08.520
Loved.

02:09.800 --> 02:11.280
In Birmingham.

02:13.040 --> 02:14.600
Because this is our city.

02:15.040 --> 02:17.720
By order of the Peaky Blinders.

02:18.000 --> 02:19.000
Get up!

02:19.400 --> 02:21.520
[crowd applauding]

02:36.240 --> 02:40.120
Now, let us sing "Immortal Invisible."

02:41.160 --> 02:43.200
[music playing]

02:45.480 --> 02:47.920
[crowd singing hymns in distance]

02:53.520 --> 02:55.320
You hear that, Grace?

02:57.280 --> 02:58.280
[door opens]

03:00.040 --> 03:02.360
The absence of my invitation
for this event

03:02.440 --> 03:05.040
was obviously an oversight
on your part, Mr. Shelby.

03:07.280 --> 03:09.440
But, look. I have the keys.

03:09.520 --> 03:11.960
I've allocated myself an office.

03:12.040 --> 03:14.560
Just there, two doors in from the street.

03:14.640 --> 03:18.880
It's the one that already has the stove
and the crucifixion on the window.

03:19.240 --> 03:20.600
Mr. Shelby?

03:21.960 --> 03:24.840
It is the one that has the crucifixion
on the window in orange and red.

03:24.920 --> 03:26.840
That will be my office.

03:27.280 --> 03:30.120
And I will take them to Saint Aloysius
for confession.

03:31.840 --> 03:33.800
You do understand

03:33.880 --> 03:36.760
these keys are part
of our broader arrangement?

03:44.040 --> 03:45.720
In the next 24 hours,

03:45.800 --> 03:48.560
you will do exactly
as you have been instructed.

03:49.160 --> 03:52.000
You'll not deviate. You'll not fail.

04:01.480 --> 04:02.880
Come on, little fellas.

04:02.960 --> 04:05.920
-Slow down. Slow down.
-[children speak indistinctly]

04:10.040 --> 04:11.560
[children laughing]

04:17.640 --> 04:19.160
The, uh…

04:20.360 --> 04:24.640
The Lord Mayor would like you
to come and eat cake and drink some tea.

04:35.840 --> 04:37.280
[sighs]

04:48.240 --> 04:50.120
[Ada] Tommy says mingle and smile.

04:50.200 --> 04:51.480
[door closes]

04:52.160 --> 04:53.640
It must be the trains.

04:53.720 --> 04:54.960
No Ruben?

04:55.040 --> 04:57.800
Do you know any other guests from London
not turned up?

04:57.880 --> 04:59.520
Some, I think, yeah.

04:59.960 --> 05:03.160
Pol, I'm paid by the company now.
So I have to talk to other people.

05:03.240 --> 05:07.600
So, you have moved from horses
to automobiles in just four years.

05:07.680 --> 05:10.120
When you ship to New York,
you pay a higher dock duty.

05:10.200 --> 05:12.240
You should consider coming with us
through Boston.

05:12.320 --> 05:15.240
I just spoke to Johnny Dogs.
He said the tunnel's hit heavy clay.

05:15.320 --> 05:16.760
-It's slowing him down.
-How long?

05:16.840 --> 05:18.480
Two days before they hit the wall.

05:18.560 --> 05:20.400
Tell him to dig a sink hole
to drain the clay.

05:20.480 --> 05:22.760
He asked if you could go down
and have a look yourself.

05:22.840 --> 05:24.600
I told him wild horses
wouldn't get you down.

05:24.680 --> 05:25.680
-Mmm.
-[Tommy sighs]

05:25.800 --> 05:29.840
Mr. Shelby, I would just like to say
that I wish I had met your dear wife

05:29.920 --> 05:31.160
before she was taken from us,

05:31.240 --> 05:35.160
and I would like to allocate an hour a day
of each of my ladies' time

05:35.240 --> 05:37.000
to make winter clothes
for the little ones.

05:37.080 --> 05:39.480
Speak to my secretary, Miss Stark,
in the gray hat.

05:39.560 --> 05:40.720
She knows my diary.

05:41.000 --> 05:43.560
Fuck me, Tom.
I don't know how you do it. Incoming.

05:43.640 --> 05:45.280
-Mr. Shelby.
-Yes?

05:45.400 --> 05:47.240
Oh, your little boy
looks so much like you.

05:47.320 --> 05:49.520
Yes. Yes. He's a little rascal, isn't he?

05:49.600 --> 05:53.120
Mr. Shelby, would it be too inconvenient
to steal you for a moment?

05:53.200 --> 05:55.160
No, no. No inconvenience at all.

05:55.240 --> 05:57.760
-Tommy, I'm sorry. He wants you.
-[baby crying]

05:57.840 --> 05:59.600
-Oh, come here, Charlie.
-Here's Daddy.

05:59.680 --> 06:01.560
Oh, little boy.

06:01.640 --> 06:03.160
-[shushing]
-So lovely to see a man

06:03.240 --> 06:05.160
willing to hold his child in public.

06:05.240 --> 06:08.400
From the members of
Moseley War Widow's Institute.

06:08.480 --> 06:10.000
What's this? What's this?

06:10.080 --> 06:12.760
Made by Mr. Winslow himself
of Winslow's Castings.

06:12.840 --> 06:13.840
Look at that.

06:13.920 --> 06:16.640
From a photograph of your horse
that ran at the Derby.

06:16.720 --> 06:18.400
Oh, that is very kind.
Thank you very much.

06:18.480 --> 06:20.520
-Grace's Secret.
-Thank you very much.

06:20.600 --> 06:21.600
-Look, Charlie.
-[crying]

06:21.680 --> 06:26.000
Would you mind holding it for us so that
we can have a photograph for the gazette?

06:27.280 --> 06:29.560
Hey. Hey. Hey.

06:30.040 --> 06:33.080
Oh, thank you. Thank you.
Thank you very much.

06:33.160 --> 06:34.760
-Thank you, Mr. Shelby.
-Not at all.

06:34.840 --> 06:36.240
-[man] Look this way.
-Thank you.

06:36.320 --> 06:37.880
-[shutter clicks]
-[women chuckling]

06:38.000 --> 06:40.040
Thank you for your time, ladies.
Thank you.

06:40.120 --> 06:42.000
Thank you for your time. Thank you.

06:42.080 --> 06:43.400
Thank you.

06:43.680 --> 06:45.800
[indistinct chatter]

06:47.960 --> 06:50.720
-Where's Charles, Ada?
-I gave him to you.

06:50.800 --> 06:52.480
-Where is he?
-I don't know.

06:53.600 --> 06:54.880
Boys.

06:55.800 --> 06:57.560
-Have you seen Charlie?
-[Arthur] Eh…

06:57.640 --> 06:59.240
I don't know. He is playing, ain't he?

06:59.320 --> 07:01.720
Pol, where's Charles?

07:02.000 --> 07:04.680
-Lizzie. Where is Charlie?
-I don't know.

07:04.760 --> 07:06.000
Where is he?

07:06.080 --> 07:07.160
Back door. Kitchen.

07:07.240 --> 07:08.840
Get to Blake Street where the cars are.

07:08.920 --> 07:11.640
Tommy. Someone said they saw a nurse
take him through the back door.

07:11.720 --> 07:12.720
-Fuck.
-What nurse?

07:12.800 --> 07:13.800
I don't know. Go.

07:15.720 --> 07:17.120
[rattling door knob]

07:21.280 --> 07:22.680
[grunting]

07:27.040 --> 07:28.120
-Arthur.
-What?

07:28.200 --> 07:30.240
Somebody saw a woman
and a kid getting into a car.

07:30.320 --> 07:31.360
Ah, fuck!

07:36.800 --> 07:38.160
Charlie!

07:38.440 --> 07:39.560
[retching]

07:40.280 --> 07:42.000
Charlie!

07:42.600 --> 07:43.680
Charlie!

07:43.760 --> 07:45.120
John.

07:46.080 --> 07:47.480
-Where is he?
-[Arthur] John!

07:47.560 --> 07:49.760
-Arthur. Arthur, where is he?
-Go find Moss!

07:49.840 --> 07:52.280
-Junctions, block them all off.
-Where is he?

07:53.040 --> 07:55.040
-Tell me.
-Someone took him.

07:55.720 --> 07:56.760
Listen to me.

07:56.840 --> 07:58.360
They put him in a car.

07:58.440 --> 08:01.240
They put him in a car and drove south.

08:01.320 --> 08:03.160
We've got road blocks, we've got spotters.

08:03.240 --> 08:04.360
I'll set up shop

08:04.440 --> 08:06.000
-and put every man we've got…
-Yeah.

08:06.080 --> 08:07.680
…between here and Maypole.

08:07.800 --> 08:09.840
-Right. You do that.
-You gotta go to the office.

08:09.920 --> 08:11.520
-Yeah.
-You gotta sit by the phone.

08:11.600 --> 08:13.560
-You do that.
-Whoever took him is going to call.

08:13.640 --> 08:14.680
Polly!

08:15.320 --> 08:16.320
Let's go, Pol.

08:17.120 --> 08:20.040
Stay by that phone.
Me and John will cover the roads.

08:20.400 --> 08:22.600
I need Michael at the Maypole junction.

08:24.120 --> 08:26.360
We need Moss to block all the roads south.

08:31.760 --> 08:32.960
Give me Moss.

08:33.640 --> 08:35.080
Gone where?

08:36.400 --> 08:37.400
[telephone dings]

08:38.240 --> 08:39.240
-[grunts]
-[clatters]

08:40.919 --> 08:42.640
-Tommy…
-It's them.

08:43.520 --> 08:44.880
-Who?
-It's fucking them.

08:44.960 --> 08:46.440
Look. It might be some random woman.

08:46.520 --> 08:48.960
-You know, sometimes women go mad…
-No, it's them.

08:49.040 --> 08:51.160
-[thunder rumbling]
-Did you break the phone?

08:56.720 --> 08:58.560
-You broke the phone.
-[door opens]

08:58.640 --> 09:00.240
It's all right, we got another phone.

09:00.320 --> 09:01.880
-[Ada] Tommy?
-Ada?

09:03.600 --> 09:05.240
There's someone outside. A priest.

09:05.360 --> 09:07.320
Stay here, Pol. Stay here.
Don't do anything.

09:09.720 --> 09:10.720
[door opens]

09:11.280 --> 09:13.360
[thunder rumbling]

09:22.040 --> 09:23.720
We have your son.

09:24.480 --> 09:26.080
Get in the car.

09:32.840 --> 09:33.840
First.

09:34.520 --> 09:35.720
Is he safe?

09:36.200 --> 09:37.720
Of course, he's safe.

09:38.120 --> 09:39.840
All children are dear to me.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.240
You have all the cards.

09:43.440 --> 09:46.560
Tell me what you want me to do
and I will certainly do it.

09:47.080 --> 09:48.920
You ever drive one of these beasts?

09:49.000 --> 09:51.080
I am asking you to conduct business.

09:51.160 --> 09:53.080
I borrowed it.

09:53.160 --> 09:54.640
Lent it. By a Lord.

09:55.280 --> 09:57.000
For the duration of this business.

09:57.080 --> 10:02.200
I will certainly do what you need me to do
with no complaints.

10:02.680 --> 10:05.400
We were forced into doing
this awful thing.

10:06.440 --> 10:10.880
We did warn you that your son would be
in danger if you deviated from the plan.

10:11.960 --> 10:13.120
You made a mistake.

10:13.200 --> 10:14.360
-You understand that?
-Yes.

10:14.440 --> 10:16.840
What mistake did you make?
Do you even know?

10:16.920 --> 10:18.680
Tell me what you want me to do.

10:19.680 --> 10:21.120
You made a deal with our enemies.

10:21.200 --> 10:22.880
I will do what needs to be done.

10:22.960 --> 10:27.520
You went behind our backs to stop
the Soviets from blowing up the train.

10:30.240 --> 10:32.360
But it's all right. It's all right.

10:32.960 --> 10:35.280
We've rectified your mistake.

10:36.080 --> 10:37.960
You ask me, "What do I need to do?"

10:38.640 --> 10:42.160
Well, here is what you need to do,
you fucking mongrel, you.

10:46.920 --> 10:50.040
But since the Bolsheviks
will not be blowing up the train,

10:50.120 --> 10:52.200
you'll blow up the train yourself.

10:53.400 --> 10:55.720
It's always been about the explosion.

10:56.320 --> 10:59.960
From the beginning. The bang. The outrage.

11:00.040 --> 11:01.320
Understand?

11:03.480 --> 11:06.960
Those are notes and fragments for you
to scatter in the wreckage,

11:07.040 --> 11:09.960
implicating named officials
from the Soviet embassy.

11:10.400 --> 11:13.360
-I will scatter them. It will be done.
-Good.

11:13.560 --> 11:16.720
Our friends at The Times
and the Daily Mail will do the rest.

11:17.040 --> 11:18.800
And once the British Government

11:18.880 --> 11:22.440
cuts diplomatic relations
with the Soviet Union,

11:22.520 --> 11:25.000
that will be our mission accomplished.

11:25.080 --> 11:27.640
You'll have been part of a fine adventure.

11:29.400 --> 11:32.600
To help with the outrage,
we need people to die in the explosion.

11:33.800 --> 11:35.080
How many?

11:36.160 --> 11:38.760
Let's say… six.

11:40.680 --> 11:43.480
Rail workers, perhaps.
Men from the factory.

11:49.760 --> 11:55.240
And I want my son returned to me
within an hour of the explosion.

11:56.640 --> 11:58.280
Oh, it's conditions now, is it?

11:58.760 --> 12:00.840
We need to fix the handover in advance.

12:00.920 --> 12:03.800
I haven't finished with you yet,
Mr. Shelby.

12:05.480 --> 12:07.880
We also hear that you're digging a tunnel.

12:09.440 --> 12:12.720
Mining for precious stones
under Wilderness House.

12:15.800 --> 12:18.440
I'm told they have a Fabergé
in the strong room.

12:19.400 --> 12:23.000
The Lilies of the Valley egg made in 1898.

12:23.800 --> 12:27.560
One of the Odd Fellows has a wife
who is obsessed with Fabergé.

12:27.640 --> 12:29.120
He wants to give it for her birthday…

12:29.200 --> 12:30.280
He will have it.

12:32.320 --> 12:35.960
And the Economic League will take
all of the jewels that you steal,

12:36.040 --> 12:38.560
to cover our considerable expenses.

12:39.440 --> 12:41.720
The fight against communism
is not cheap, you know?

12:42.520 --> 12:45.360
-So, if you want to see your…
-I will give you all the jewels.

12:46.880 --> 12:48.600
A bang first.

12:49.280 --> 12:53.040
Then bring everything you've stolen
to your office at dawn.

12:53.960 --> 12:55.960
No. No.

12:56.480 --> 12:58.880
I'll not be able to get the jewels
to you by dawn.

12:58.960 --> 13:00.000
The tunnel has hit clay.

13:00.080 --> 13:04.160
If the St. Andrew's clock strikes
5:00 a.m. on the night of the robbery

13:04.240 --> 13:06.800
and we don't have
everything that we asked for,

13:06.880 --> 13:08.680
the bell will be tolling for your boy.

13:08.760 --> 13:11.200
[thunder rumbling]

13:12.040 --> 13:14.160
Now, get out of my fucking car.

13:16.760 --> 13:17.760
[exhales]

13:27.720 --> 13:29.320
-[Tommy] Where's Linda?
-With Esme.

13:29.400 --> 13:31.280
Esme's waters broke.

13:31.360 --> 13:34.120
I was just with her.
Running around fucking broke the waters.

13:34.200 --> 13:35.240
Where's Finn?

13:35.320 --> 13:37.360
Out with the young'uns
looking for the Riley.

13:37.440 --> 13:38.520
We couldn't reach him.

13:38.600 --> 13:39.760
I need to know who spoke.

13:39.960 --> 13:41.640
Our enemies know everything. Everything.

13:42.480 --> 13:45.680
I need to know who spoke
about business outside of the family.

13:45.760 --> 13:48.280
I need to know who spoke
and who they spoke to. Now.

13:48.400 --> 13:50.520
-Tommy…
-Your wife, Arthur?

13:52.960 --> 13:56.440
I'm gonna tell myself
that you're not thinking straight.

13:57.640 --> 13:59.240
Your mind's not clear.

13:59.880 --> 14:02.760
Or Esme getting cash
for cocaine, eh, John?

14:03.040 --> 14:04.080
Fuck!

14:04.720 --> 14:06.720
All of a sudden,
back in the family, Ada, eh.

14:06.920 --> 14:08.760
That's a surprise. Out of the blue.

14:09.520 --> 14:10.600
On whose orders?

14:10.680 --> 14:12.560
Tommy, this is not helping find him.

14:12.640 --> 14:14.480
And you and your painter.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.120
You said he knows you.

14:16.680 --> 14:19.000
Things developed. You talked.

14:19.640 --> 14:23.440
If anyone has talked
about the tunnel to anyone else,

14:23.520 --> 14:25.600
I need to know,
and I need to know this second.

14:25.680 --> 14:27.560
-What about your clay kickers?
-[Arthur] Mmm.

14:28.080 --> 14:29.360
Drunk in a pub.

14:29.440 --> 14:31.240
I trust those men with my life.

14:31.320 --> 14:32.600
More than you trust us?

14:32.680 --> 14:34.120
Yeah.

14:34.200 --> 14:35.480
As of an hour ago, yes.

14:36.280 --> 14:38.160
[John] Where's Michael
in this lineup anyway?

14:38.240 --> 14:39.720
-[Polly] Leave Michael out.
-Yeah?

14:39.800 --> 14:41.520
-He should be here.
-I don't even know him.

14:41.600 --> 14:43.600
How long you known him?
Fucking three years?

14:43.680 --> 14:45.080
[Polly] He's not your whipping boy.

14:45.160 --> 14:46.880
I don't even fucking know the boy.

14:47.440 --> 14:49.880
I never told Michael
about the Lilies of the Valley.

14:51.640 --> 14:55.560
The only people I told
about the Fabergé eggs are in this room.

15:00.800 --> 15:03.080
Tommy, I want you to know
that I came back for love.

15:06.360 --> 15:07.840
And common sense.

15:13.360 --> 15:15.600
And Esme's got no need for extra cash.

15:17.440 --> 15:19.800
[door opens and closes]

15:21.240 --> 15:23.040
You bring my wife into this.

15:24.240 --> 15:26.800
Means we speak when this business is done.

15:32.080 --> 15:36.280
John, Arthur,
I need 50 sticks of BSA dynamite,

15:36.360 --> 15:41.040
300 yards of cable
and six detonators by midday tomorrow.

15:42.520 --> 15:44.320
This is evidence.
I need you to scatter it.

15:45.480 --> 15:47.720
We're blowing up a train
and people are gonna die.

16:01.680 --> 16:03.760
[door opens and closes]

16:05.480 --> 16:07.640
Ruben and I talked about many things.

16:10.920 --> 16:13.080
-But not that. Not ever.
-[door opens and closes]

16:14.480 --> 16:16.160
Tommy. I'm sorry I'm late.

16:16.240 --> 16:18.600
We looked everywhere.
All the way up to Hay Mills.

16:18.680 --> 16:20.200
So, nothing.

16:20.280 --> 16:23.960
Put four cans of petrol
in the boot of my car and bring it around.

16:24.040 --> 16:25.800
And put cigarettes and a lamp in the box.

16:26.160 --> 16:27.320
Fetch Michael. I need him.

16:30.040 --> 16:32.200
Ada told me he gave you red wine.

16:32.600 --> 16:34.960
I imagine you can't remember
half of what you talked about.

16:35.040 --> 16:36.640
He was never interested in business.

16:38.200 --> 16:40.960
He came to you at my wedding.

16:42.600 --> 16:45.080
He pursued you. Sought you out.

16:46.680 --> 16:49.960
Why would an educated man of his standing
do something like that?

16:53.160 --> 16:54.960
You mean, to a woman like me?

16:55.040 --> 16:56.120
Yes.

17:00.680 --> 17:02.280
I've done the odds on all of you.

17:02.360 --> 17:03.560
Evens it's him.

17:05.400 --> 17:07.800
There's another possibility.
But evens it's him.

17:14.720 --> 17:16.520
[door opens and slams shut]

17:19.160 --> 17:20.160
[Polly sniffling]

17:21.119 --> 17:22.920
[Polly sobbing]

17:44.680 --> 17:45.680
[screams]

18:14.400 --> 18:15.400
[Alfie grunts]

18:24.760 --> 18:26.480
I asked you to come alone and unarmed.

18:26.560 --> 18:29.040
Yeah, well, alone I ain't never gonna do,
am I?

18:29.120 --> 18:32.280
And as for the cane, don't worry about it.
That is just my sciatica.

18:32.360 --> 18:36.000
It always plays up around the winter
and the summer solstice.

18:36.360 --> 18:37.960
What have you got for me, Alfie?

18:38.040 --> 18:39.400
What did you bring me here for?

18:39.720 --> 18:42.200
It's on the way to somewhere
I need to be in a hurry.

18:42.280 --> 18:44.320
-Huh.
-What have you got for me?

18:44.440 --> 18:48.240
Well, seeing as you was prepared
to pay such an exorbitant amount

18:48.320 --> 18:52.560
for this information,
I decided to give you value for money.

18:52.640 --> 18:56.680
So, here are the names
of all the men in England

18:56.800 --> 19:00.600
whom I would approach, right,
if I had a Fabergé egg for sale.

19:00.680 --> 19:02.080
There you go.

19:02.400 --> 19:05.800
And then, here's all the men
on that list, you know,

19:05.880 --> 19:07.400
who would buy the old Fabergé egg

19:07.480 --> 19:10.120
even if they knew
that that item was stolen, eh.

19:11.200 --> 19:14.480
Then in come your curious
fucking gyppo question.

19:14.560 --> 19:16.880
I won't ask, but, um…

19:17.000 --> 19:21.640
Here is a list of the men
who would buy a Fabergé

19:21.720 --> 19:24.040
because of their wife's obsession.

19:33.160 --> 19:37.280
Oh, yes. Thank you, Mr. Shelby.
Lovely doing business with you.

19:52.960 --> 19:53.960
[gun clicks]

19:55.160 --> 19:56.600
You left a name off the list, Alfie.

19:56.680 --> 19:58.000
-Did I?
-Yeah.

19:58.320 --> 20:00.520
I've already spoken to my people
in the jewelry quarter,

20:00.600 --> 20:02.240
experienced dealers.

20:02.920 --> 20:05.880
They tell me there are only three men
in Britain

20:05.960 --> 20:07.960
whose wives are obsessed with Fabergé.

20:08.040 --> 20:09.560
Makes them good customers.

20:09.800 --> 20:11.440
You missed the richest one off the list.

20:11.520 --> 20:13.640
Yeah, well, if you knew already,

20:13.720 --> 20:16.800
how come you dragged me all the way
out into the fucking oggin, mate?

20:16.880 --> 20:19.040
Two reasons. Reason one,

20:19.680 --> 20:22.400
by withholding a name
that you most certainly know,

20:23.000 --> 20:24.640
you've proven you have done a deal

20:24.720 --> 20:26.320
with the Odd Fellows.

20:26.800 --> 20:29.560
It was you who told them about the tunnel.

20:29.640 --> 20:32.800
You who told them
about the fucking deal with the Soviets.

20:33.960 --> 20:35.360
Reason two,

20:35.440 --> 20:38.200
the name of the man
that you are withholding must be my enemy

20:38.280 --> 20:40.280
otherwise you wouldn't be protecting him.

20:40.760 --> 20:42.440
He's now a man I can use.

20:42.880 --> 20:45.280
Listen, sweetie, you can't take a man--

20:45.360 --> 20:48.240
You gave information
in exchange for a share.

20:48.320 --> 20:52.840
Tommy, there were things in that treasury
that God himself, he spoke to me.

20:52.920 --> 20:55.160
He said, "Alfie, you are meant
to have these things."

20:55.240 --> 20:56.440
You crossed the line, Alfie.

20:57.040 --> 20:59.000
-You fucking what?
-You crossed the line.

20:59.080 --> 21:01.400
-The line?
-They're using my boy!

21:07.120 --> 21:08.400
Did you fucking know?

21:08.480 --> 21:10.280
Yeah, I knew, you know.

21:10.360 --> 21:14.200
But damned as I am,
it made no fucking difference to me mate.

21:15.440 --> 21:16.440
[grunting]

21:20.520 --> 21:21.560
[Alfie choking]

21:21.640 --> 21:23.040
Fucking hell, Tommy.

21:23.760 --> 21:24.760
[gun clicks]

21:26.520 --> 21:28.440
[Alfie] Oh, for crying out loud.

21:28.520 --> 21:30.400
What the fuck is going on?

21:34.760 --> 21:37.400
What is the matter with you,
Tommy, eh? Eh?

21:37.800 --> 21:39.120
You got fucking angry, ain't you?

21:39.200 --> 21:41.240
-Yeah, I got angry…
-It's in your head, mate!

21:41.320 --> 21:44.080
Tommy, I know this bastard deserves it!

21:45.080 --> 21:46.920
It's in your fucking head, mate!

21:47.000 --> 21:51.080
I know this bastard deserves it!
I fucking know!

21:51.160 --> 21:52.640
But if you kill him now,

21:52.720 --> 21:55.760
the truce with the London outfits
will be blown to fucking pieces,

21:55.840 --> 21:56.880
-all right?
-Michael.

21:56.960 --> 22:00.600
Don't worry about that truce, kid, right,
'cause it fell apart.

22:02.680 --> 22:04.040
You got nothing to worry about

22:04.120 --> 22:05.840
when it comes to the old
scary London boys.

22:05.920 --> 22:07.400
Which fucking side are you on, Alfie?

22:07.480 --> 22:09.920
I do not give a fuck
right now, kid, right?

22:12.760 --> 22:17.520
I do not want him to spare me
because of some fucking peace pact!

22:18.880 --> 22:24.840
I want him to acknowledge
that his anger is un-fucking-justified!

22:25.760 --> 22:29.440
I want him to acknowledge
that he who fights by the sword,

22:29.520 --> 22:31.480
he fucking dies by it, Tommy.

22:32.400 --> 22:34.440
So, what, they took your boy,
did they, eh?

22:35.280 --> 22:36.320
They got your boy?

22:36.400 --> 22:39.400
And what fucking line
am I supposed to have crossed?

22:42.840 --> 22:45.880
How many fathers, right,
how many sons, yeah,

22:46.000 --> 22:50.640
have you cut, killed, murdered,
fucking butchered, innocent and guilty,

22:50.720 --> 22:52.640
to send straight to fucking hell,
ain't ya?

22:52.720 --> 22:54.200
Just like me!

22:55.560 --> 22:57.240
You fucking stand there,

22:58.080 --> 22:59.680
you judging me,

22:59.760 --> 23:04.240
stand there and talk to me
about crossing some fucking line.

23:06.600 --> 23:08.880
If you pull that trigger, right,

23:08.960 --> 23:12.040
you pull that trigger
for a fucking honorable reason.

23:12.120 --> 23:16.080
Like an honorable man,
not like some fucking civilian

23:16.160 --> 23:21.040
that does not understand
the wicked way of our world, mate.

23:23.120 --> 23:28.000
Look, Tommy, the killing of Alfie Solomons
is not going to help.

23:30.000 --> 23:32.400
It'll be very bad for business.

23:35.720 --> 23:37.000
Michael…

23:40.080 --> 23:41.920
go and call Inspector Moss.

23:42.000 --> 23:43.800
Tell him it's Palmer.

23:50.440 --> 23:52.400
Well said, Alfie.

23:53.080 --> 23:54.560
Well said.

23:56.960 --> 23:57.960
[groans]

24:01.080 --> 24:03.040
I did not know about your boy, though.

24:03.480 --> 24:05.080
I know.

24:05.600 --> 24:07.120
I saw.

24:27.480 --> 24:28.520
[Ruben] Hello?

24:53.400 --> 24:54.400
[gun cocks]

24:58.280 --> 24:59.480
Good Lord.

25:07.560 --> 25:08.680
Polly.

25:10.840 --> 25:12.520
Why didn't you come?

25:14.080 --> 25:16.360
I was going to get on the train last night
but then I…

25:17.920 --> 25:20.960
I realized I simply wasn't ready
to enter your world.

25:23.120 --> 25:24.240
Good God. I'm shaking.

25:24.320 --> 25:25.320
Good.

25:28.080 --> 25:32.000
Right now, I'm ready.
I have been searching all night for you.

25:33.360 --> 25:36.240
Polly, whatever you've been told,
it's not true.

25:41.160 --> 25:42.920
[breathing heavily]

25:53.240 --> 25:54.920
The painting was wrong.

26:00.160 --> 26:02.680
She was too sure of herself.

26:06.200 --> 26:07.560
I'm not.

26:11.240 --> 26:12.800
Not anymore.

26:15.680 --> 26:17.440
I can paint another.

26:20.480 --> 26:22.240
[sobbing and sniffling]

26:22.440 --> 26:23.760
Polly.

26:27.600 --> 26:29.600
What the fuck am I doing?

26:34.800 --> 26:38.200
I want a dull life. I want you.

26:38.440 --> 26:40.600
I want you. I want you.

26:40.680 --> 26:45.560
I want you to paint me
in a dress that I bought in a shop.

26:47.480 --> 26:48.920
We have a life?

26:52.480 --> 26:53.840
I think so.

26:58.320 --> 26:59.960
[telephone ringing]

27:02.400 --> 27:03.680
Hello?

27:06.840 --> 27:07.840
[receiver dings]

27:13.160 --> 27:17.080
I demand to see my solicitor!
I have my right to have him here!

27:17.160 --> 27:20.680
Gilbert Palmer, I want to talk to you
about a missing kid.

27:20.960 --> 27:22.280
[grunting]

27:22.640 --> 27:25.480
We are Peaky Blinders.

27:26.120 --> 27:27.440
Where is he?

27:27.760 --> 27:29.960
-Deep breath.
-[muffled breathing]

27:30.240 --> 27:31.520
Where is he?

27:31.760 --> 27:33.400
[birds cawing]

27:35.240 --> 27:36.480
[car approaching]

27:51.520 --> 27:53.240
[shouting indistinctly]

27:53.640 --> 27:55.320
What the fuck
are you doing here, Tommy?

27:55.400 --> 27:56.760
They've taken my boy, Johnny.

27:56.840 --> 27:58.400
Everything's fucking changed.

27:58.480 --> 28:00.560
I have to get the hole dug
before midnight.

28:00.640 --> 28:01.800
Do you hear me?

28:02.640 --> 28:04.640
Are you not going after Charles yourself?

28:04.720 --> 28:06.120
Tommy!

28:40.960 --> 28:42.000
[Michael] I was, uh…

28:43.600 --> 28:46.360
This morning
I was out on the road with Tommy.

28:48.520 --> 28:49.760
I killed a man.

28:50.680 --> 28:52.840
He needed cover. I was all he had.

28:53.880 --> 28:55.760
What did he give you?

28:57.920 --> 28:59.960
He said it's good for close range.

29:00.840 --> 29:02.240
You're better with my gun.

29:02.320 --> 29:04.000
No, no, this is mine now.

29:05.440 --> 29:07.080
Feels part of me hand.

29:08.680 --> 29:10.000
Where'd you hit him?

29:11.480 --> 29:12.840
I hit him in the side of the head.

29:12.920 --> 29:14.480
How was you when he went down?

29:14.560 --> 29:15.960
Tommy said I did all right.

29:17.280 --> 29:19.440
This is where we think
Charles is being held.

29:22.280 --> 29:26.360
They're not expecting nobody,
so you should be alone.

29:33.960 --> 29:35.520
There's two good men there.

29:37.360 --> 29:38.880
You do what they say.

29:40.480 --> 29:42.640
But I fire the bullet. All right?

29:43.800 --> 29:45.360
Yes, you can be there.

29:46.160 --> 29:47.920
But it's better if I do it.

29:48.920 --> 29:51.200
See, these are experienced men, Michael.

29:54.960 --> 29:56.920
When you're sure the kid's safe,

29:57.760 --> 29:59.160
you call Finn.

30:00.040 --> 30:01.440
All right.

30:08.400 --> 30:09.960
Come on, boys.

30:16.560 --> 30:17.600
[door closing]

30:37.520 --> 30:39.480
[Hughes] Ah, hello, there.

30:42.040 --> 30:44.400
Here you go. How's that?

30:45.040 --> 30:47.360
You like a spoon? A shiny spoon?

30:48.000 --> 30:49.840
Do you want to hold the spoon there?

30:51.600 --> 30:52.640
[grunting]

31:00.760 --> 31:01.800
[indistinct chatter]

31:01.880 --> 31:03.800
[man] All out, boys!

31:03.920 --> 31:05.840
Wild cat strike!

31:06.000 --> 31:07.400
[indistinct yelling]

31:15.120 --> 31:17.440
This locomotive…

31:19.960 --> 31:23.440
couples in 15 minutes.

31:24.840 --> 31:27.880
If we do not hear word by 10:00…
[sniffs]

31:29.920 --> 31:31.080
we blow it up.

31:33.680 --> 31:35.600
There's men on board, Arthur.

31:36.800 --> 31:38.080
Yeah.

31:38.160 --> 31:40.080
Six men on board, Charlie.

31:40.760 --> 31:42.040
Driver,

31:42.720 --> 31:43.920
stoker,

31:45.280 --> 31:47.160
and four men I handpicked myself.

31:51.920 --> 31:53.680
Me and John picked those men.

31:56.560 --> 31:59.400
It is me and John
who will pull the switch.

32:05.200 --> 32:07.200
The rest of you men can go home.

32:08.840 --> 32:09.880
[train whistle blowing]

32:12.240 --> 32:14.080
[William] Tommy. Tommy.

32:14.320 --> 32:16.600
-He's got the shakes. Help me with him.
-[Tommy grunts]

32:18.040 --> 32:19.920
Get him out. Get him out!

32:20.080 --> 32:21.200
Bringing him through.

32:21.400 --> 32:23.200
We need to move. Now!

32:26.400 --> 32:28.120
[steam whooshing]

32:47.480 --> 32:48.520
[train screeches]

32:59.040 --> 33:00.080
[engine stops]

33:02.160 --> 33:03.680
You wait here.

33:05.760 --> 33:07.320
I will do the killing.

33:10.800 --> 33:12.520
That's a fucking order.

33:35.520 --> 33:36.560
[grunts]

33:38.680 --> 33:40.120
You move too fast, Thomas.

33:43.120 --> 33:44.680
[rumbling]

33:49.760 --> 33:51.840
-We need more timber.
-Then make it safe.

33:51.920 --> 33:54.080
-I'll go on.
-Thomas, it's too fucking wet.

33:54.160 --> 33:55.880
-It's sludge.
-Make it fucking safe!

33:56.360 --> 33:57.880
-And I'll go on!
-[sighs]

33:59.280 --> 34:00.440
Okay.

34:04.480 --> 34:06.400
[breathing heavily]

34:32.600 --> 34:34.760
[panting]

34:45.239 --> 34:46.280
[blows air]

34:52.480 --> 34:53.520
[baby whimpering]

34:57.240 --> 34:58.280
[gun cocks]

35:00.920 --> 35:02.360
[panting]

35:05.320 --> 35:07.160
What do you think you're doing, boy?

35:12.000 --> 35:13.280
Please don't.

35:14.600 --> 35:17.280
-Please don't shoot. Please don't shoot.
-[baby whimpers]

35:18.320 --> 35:20.400
Please don't. Please.

35:21.040 --> 35:22.080
[grunts]

35:33.040 --> 35:34.760
-You fucking rat.
-[Michael groans]

35:36.080 --> 35:38.360
-What do you think you're doing?
-[grunting]

35:38.440 --> 35:40.440
You know who you're fucking messing with?

35:41.480 --> 35:42.520
[groaning and choking]

35:44.560 --> 35:45.600
[train whistling]

35:57.960 --> 35:59.560
We don't have much time.

35:59.640 --> 36:02.640
I'm gonna take your fucking life from you.

36:08.240 --> 36:09.520
Let's go!

36:10.160 --> 36:11.200
[Tommy grunts]

36:19.720 --> 36:21.760
You're a gypsy bastard.

36:21.920 --> 36:22.960
-[grunts]
-[screams]

36:42.000 --> 36:43.040
[train honking]

36:43.120 --> 36:45.120
Who wants to be in heaven, eh?

36:45.200 --> 36:46.560
[train chugging]

36:46.640 --> 36:50.800
Who wants to be in heaven when you can be
sending men to fucking hell. [chuckles]

36:51.000 --> 36:52.320
Hey.

36:53.080 --> 36:56.800
I'll do it, Arthur, eh. I'll do it.

36:57.320 --> 36:58.360
Get up!

36:59.280 --> 37:00.640
-I'll take him!
-No!

37:01.680 --> 37:02.960
This bastard's mine.

37:03.240 --> 37:04.440
Go call Finn.

37:07.720 --> 37:09.360
I told Tommy I'll do it.

37:11.160 --> 37:12.520
So, I'll do it.

37:13.400 --> 37:14.440
[Hughes grunts]

37:18.680 --> 37:20.120
[Michael panting]

37:22.920 --> 37:23.960
[telephone ringing]

37:26.280 --> 37:27.920
Arthur, wait!

37:28.000 --> 37:29.400
Charlie's safe.

37:29.480 --> 37:30.520
[exploding]

37:34.000 --> 37:35.320
[Finn] Fuck!

37:35.800 --> 37:37.560
[train wreck clattering and shattering]

37:59.880 --> 38:00.920
[grunts]

38:11.080 --> 38:12.120
[panting]

38:23.000 --> 38:24.040
[chuckles]

38:26.840 --> 38:28.760
-It's all right.
-[baby coos]

38:46.920 --> 38:47.960
[baby crying]

38:54.080 --> 38:55.120
Oh…

38:55.760 --> 38:57.760
[baby continues crying]

39:24.920 --> 39:25.960
[whirring]

39:27.080 --> 39:28.480
Let me speak to him.

39:29.160 --> 39:30.680
-Hello, Charlie.
-[baby mumbling]

39:31.800 --> 39:33.040
Hello, Charlie.

39:34.280 --> 39:35.880
Can you hear me?

39:36.080 --> 39:37.360
Yeah.

39:39.280 --> 39:40.920
Yeah, you go to bed.

39:41.840 --> 39:42.960
Good boy.

39:53.840 --> 39:54.880
[sobbing]

40:21.840 --> 40:23.520
Where the hell have you been?

40:25.240 --> 40:27.000
I've been out in Maypole.

40:28.480 --> 40:29.960
There's been some trouble.

40:33.320 --> 40:34.760
I can't stay.

40:40.080 --> 40:41.440
You can't stay?

40:43.480 --> 40:44.960
Tommy needs my help.

40:47.120 --> 40:48.400
It's family business.

40:48.480 --> 40:50.240
No. No. Please.

40:50.320 --> 40:51.440
I'm sorry.

40:51.520 --> 40:52.800
Please.

40:53.040 --> 40:54.440
[breathing heavily]

41:24.880 --> 41:25.920
Where is he?

41:26.000 --> 41:27.240
[Ada] He's upstairs.

42:29.120 --> 42:32.280
Mr. Shelby, this is Monsieur Silk.

42:33.400 --> 42:35.880
He is here on behalf
of the Parisian buyers.

42:36.200 --> 42:38.080
He needs to verify the value.

42:41.880 --> 42:44.520
It was a pleasure doing business with you
these past few months.

42:55.440 --> 42:57.840
You would never steal from your family,
would you? [chuckles]

43:01.000 --> 43:03.000
The collection
was mostly my mother's anyway.

43:03.760 --> 43:05.280
It was more mine than theirs.

43:05.360 --> 43:08.960
And they would never have sold it.
They would have wasted it on a lost cause.

43:09.360 --> 43:11.040
You needed a tunnel.

43:12.880 --> 43:15.200
I need your signature
to make this sale legal.

43:15.760 --> 43:20.760
[Silk] Confirmed, the original
Duke Alexander Petrovich's collection.

43:23.800 --> 43:26.840
To raise a legal bill of sale
and get this across the border,

43:27.760 --> 43:31.840
I need authorization signed by yourself

43:31.920 --> 43:34.600
in the family name, in my presence.

43:34.680 --> 43:36.400
As we agreed,

43:36.480 --> 43:38.520
half for the tunnel,
half for the signature.

43:40.120 --> 43:41.160
Where will you go?

43:41.480 --> 43:42.880
Vienna.

43:44.480 --> 43:46.800
-There is a man waiting for me.
-[Tommy chuckles]

43:47.320 --> 43:48.560
Poor man.

43:49.080 --> 43:50.320
You?

43:50.760 --> 43:51.800
Birmingham.

43:53.080 --> 43:54.640
I'm going to buy a racehorse,

43:57.200 --> 43:58.840
have it trained.

44:27.760 --> 44:31.200
Also, £5,000 for the sex.

44:50.200 --> 44:53.000
And £5,000 for helping you
through the grief of losing your wife.

45:03.920 --> 45:06.400
You didn't even come close.

45:07.960 --> 45:10.600
[Silk clears throat]
The papers are in order.

45:11.760 --> 45:14.120
Now, I just need your signature
for the provenance.

45:14.200 --> 45:16.680
Of course. I have a pen.

45:28.120 --> 45:30.520
At home, these jewels saw way worse.

45:31.680 --> 45:33.800
That's why they are all cursed.

45:34.960 --> 45:38.040
As are we, Mr. Shelby.

45:41.560 --> 45:43.440
If you're ever in Vienna, look me up.

46:10.920 --> 46:12.320
[door opens and closes]

46:56.040 --> 46:57.520
Before I begin,

46:59.840 --> 47:01.800
I want to let you know
I made a mistake.

47:06.600 --> 47:08.240
I made a mistake

47:09.120 --> 47:11.200
and I want to apologize to all of you.

47:13.400 --> 47:14.440
Arthur,

47:15.240 --> 47:18.120
you warned me against getting involved
in Russian business.

47:19.800 --> 47:20.880
And you were right.

47:21.600 --> 47:22.640
Mmm.

47:23.720 --> 47:25.160
I doubted your wife.

47:25.800 --> 47:27.320
For that I'm sorry.

47:28.160 --> 47:32.320
Linda, I have added £3,000 here
in the hope that you'll forgive me.

47:42.120 --> 47:43.720
Apology accepted.

47:48.680 --> 47:50.480
Esme, I doubted you as well.

47:50.920 --> 47:53.280
Now John's got innocent lives
on his conscience.

47:54.120 --> 47:56.640
-Ordinary working men--
-Yeah, all right, Esme. Got it.

47:56.720 --> 47:58.800
No, she's right.

47:59.520 --> 48:01.640
You and Arthur
are gonna have to share that burden.

48:05.240 --> 48:07.680
But I hope
the house that you can buy with this

48:07.760 --> 48:11.560
can become a place of contemplation.

48:13.440 --> 48:15.080
Perhaps redemption.

48:19.960 --> 48:24.880
Charlie, for lost tools, dangerous goods
and Curly's wise words.

48:25.640 --> 48:28.440
Johnny, for board and lodgings.

48:30.440 --> 48:32.040
Lizzie.

48:38.240 --> 48:39.560
Michael,

48:40.200 --> 48:41.480
for the killings.

48:42.880 --> 48:44.800
£5,000 each for the cutting
and the shooting.

48:44.880 --> 48:46.600
-No, Tommy…
-What?

48:46.680 --> 48:48.040
Tell me, eh!

48:48.720 --> 48:50.280
This is who I am!

48:51.920 --> 48:55.200
And this is all I can give you
for what you given me.

48:55.760 --> 48:58.240
Your hearts and your souls.

49:02.240 --> 49:05.960
Yesterday I nearly lost my son.

49:07.560 --> 49:09.560
You should fucking understand that.

49:11.960 --> 49:13.640
For what, eh?

49:13.840 --> 49:16.760
For what? For this? For this? [chuckles]

49:19.080 --> 49:22.240
And I know you all want me to say
that I'll change.

49:22.320 --> 49:24.000
That this fucking business will change.

49:24.080 --> 49:26.680
But I've learnt something
in the last few days.

49:26.760 --> 49:30.240
Those bastards, those bastards

49:31.880 --> 49:33.560
are worse than us!

49:34.760 --> 49:38.160
Politicians, fucking Judges,
Lords and Ladies.

49:38.240 --> 49:39.600
They are worse than us.

49:39.680 --> 49:43.160
And they will never admit us
to their palaces

49:43.400 --> 49:46.120
no matter how legitimate we become.

49:46.960 --> 49:48.560
Because of who we are.

49:48.960 --> 49:51.760
Because of who we fucking are,
because of where we're fucking from.

49:51.840 --> 49:53.080
Isn't that right, Ada?

49:54.040 --> 49:55.520
Our Ada knows.

49:56.600 --> 49:58.680
She got smart about the revolution.

49:59.120 --> 50:02.440
And she knows you have to get
what you want your own way.

50:05.800 --> 50:10.640
Lizzie, I want it known
that money was for you

50:10.720 --> 50:15.720
because some nights it was you
who stopped my heart from breaking.

50:16.040 --> 50:17.360
No one else.

50:21.280 --> 50:23.320
And the rest of you,
you took the King's shilling.

50:27.120 --> 50:29.000
You took the King's fucking shilling.

50:30.320 --> 50:34.160
When you take the King's shilling,
the King expects you to kill.

50:36.600 --> 50:37.840
Right, Arthur?

50:38.880 --> 50:40.280
Yeah.

50:40.560 --> 50:42.800
That's how it works. Right, John?

50:49.360 --> 50:50.880
That's right.

50:52.000 --> 50:53.800
That's right, Pol.

50:55.280 --> 50:56.760
That's fucking right.

51:01.000 --> 51:02.040
Tommy,

51:04.120 --> 51:05.560
you've had a bad time.

51:06.640 --> 51:07.960
We understand.

51:10.720 --> 51:13.040
So at an alternative time,

51:16.480 --> 51:17.800
when we have all recovered,

51:19.600 --> 51:23.560
I would like to put before the family

51:24.520 --> 51:26.200
an alternative view

51:27.720 --> 51:30.960
of the future
of the Shelby Company Limited.

51:33.520 --> 51:35.240
A more hopeful view.

51:37.920 --> 51:39.760
[baby crying]

51:40.760 --> 51:42.880
Which I, for one,
would quite like to hear.

51:43.760 --> 51:44.960
As would I.

51:45.680 --> 51:47.160
As would I.

51:54.160 --> 51:55.560
[Linda] Come on, Arthur.

51:56.040 --> 51:58.200
The train for the dock leaves in one hour.

51:59.160 --> 52:03.880
Then we get the boat to New York
and it'll all be in the past.

52:39.120 --> 52:41.080
I'll be off then, Tom.

52:42.720 --> 52:43.760
[Arthur sniffles]

52:47.160 --> 52:48.440
I'll see you, eh?

52:51.520 --> 52:53.080
I'll see you, brother.

53:03.120 --> 53:04.440
Bye, Curly.

53:06.560 --> 53:08.440
You can go, but you won't get far, Arthur.

53:09.880 --> 53:10.920
Uh…

53:11.200 --> 53:12.360
All right, Tom.

53:12.440 --> 53:14.040
I spoke to Moss last night.

53:15.760 --> 53:18.160
He told me
that the Chief Constable of Birmingham

53:18.240 --> 53:21.000
has issued a warrant for your arrest.

53:21.840 --> 53:26.360
Murder, sedition,
conspiracy to cause explosion.

53:27.600 --> 53:30.040
John, they're coming for you as well.

53:30.640 --> 53:33.920
Murder, conspiracy to cause explosion.

53:34.880 --> 53:36.640
-Michael…
-[Arthur] What the fuck?

53:36.720 --> 53:38.080
…for the murder of Hughes.

53:38.840 --> 53:40.200
Polly…

53:41.640 --> 53:44.080
Wait a minute.
What the fuck are you talking…

53:44.160 --> 53:46.560
…the murder
of Chief Inspector Chester Campbell.

53:46.680 --> 53:47.960
[clamoring]

53:48.160 --> 53:50.800
The people that we betrayed last night,
they want to bring us down.

53:50.880 --> 53:53.040
-They control the police…
-[knock on door]

53:53.120 --> 53:54.520
…they control the judges,

53:54.600 --> 53:55.920
they control the juries,

53:56.000 --> 53:57.360
they control the jails.

53:57.440 --> 54:00.720
But they do not control
the elected government.

54:00.800 --> 54:02.800
-Listen to me!
-Why didn't you tell us before?

54:02.920 --> 54:04.280
-You are my brother!
-Listen to me.

54:04.360 --> 54:06.240
So I've made a deal…

54:06.320 --> 54:09.080
-They'll hang us!
-…in return for giving evidence

54:09.200 --> 54:11.160
-against them.
-[Arthur] We'll fucking hang.

54:11.240 --> 54:12.600
It's all taken care of.

54:12.680 --> 54:15.640
Lizzie, collect up the money
and bring it to the cellar.

54:16.160 --> 54:19.120
You will all get your money in due course.

54:19.520 --> 54:21.640
When the police get in, do not resist.

54:21.720 --> 54:23.840
You go with them,
you do not say anything.

54:24.880 --> 54:30.120
Arthur, I've made a deal with people
even more powerful than our enemies.

54:30.200 --> 54:31.440
-[Linda] Arthur!
-Trust me.

54:31.720 --> 54:33.720
[indistinct screaming and clamoring]

54:34.000 --> 54:35.320
Trust me.

54:35.800 --> 54:37.600
You did this deliberately!

54:38.160 --> 54:40.520
You made this happen to keep us!

54:40.600 --> 54:42.520
-Come here. Come here.
-[Linda screaming]

54:42.600 --> 54:44.840
Come on now. We have to run.

54:45.400 --> 54:48.840
[indistinct yelling and screaming]

54:50.320 --> 54:51.960
[Arthur] Fuck you!

54:52.600 --> 54:55.480
[indistinct screaming and yelling]

56:46.120 --> 56:48.120
[theme song playing]
